  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Urban Water Management: Climate action &amp; circular economy transition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Half of humanity now lives in urban areas.  Cities are facing increasingly severe water challenges in meeting water demands for growing urban populations. Climate change is exacerbating water challenges in human settlements through changes in the water cycle, affecting the availability and quality of water resources and increasing water-related disasters. Addressing these water challenges is key to the sustainability of cities and urban areas. To meet water challenges in human settlements, a holistic approach under the Integrated Urban Water Management (IUWM) framework is essential.
The activity supports Member States in water security and climate adaptation and resilience in human settlements (urban and rural) by promoting Integrated Urban Water Management and circular economy approaches through: knowledge generation and dissemination; promotion of innovative approaches and technologies, effective governance models, and institutional frameworks for urban water management; sharing of best practices; capacity needs assessment, and scientific cooperation among cities and stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
